-- title:
--   Uniqueness of places over a point smooth in the first variable
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $N$ a positive integer, and let `data` consist of a bivariate integral polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic in the outer variable $Y$, of degree $\psi(N)=\sum_{d\mid N,\ d\text{ squarefree}} N/d$ in $Y$, and annihilates the pair $(j(q), j(q^N))$ of $q$-expansions. Write $\bar\Phi$ for the image of $\Phi$ under coefficientwise reduction into $k$, and let $s,t \in k$ satisfy: $\bar\Phi$ evaluated at inner variable $s$ and outer variable $t$ is $0$; and the derivative in the outer variable of the variable-exchanged polynomial `swapBivar` $\bar\Phi$, evaluated at inner variable $t$ and outer variable $s$, is non-zero — that is, $\partial\bar\Phi/\partial X$ does not vanish at $(s,t)$. Let $F = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ be the $k$-subfield of the Laurent series field $k((q))$ generated by $\tilde j = q^{-1}\,\overline{E_4^3\eta^{-24}}$ and by $\tilde j_N$, its image under $q \mapsto q^N$. Let $P$ and $Q$ be places of $F$ over $k$, i.e. proper valuation subrings of $F$ containing $k$ whose ideals are principal, with $\mathrm{ord}$ the associated normalised valuation. If $\mathrm{ord}_P(\tilde j - s) > 0$, $\mathrm{ord}_P(\tilde j_N - t) > 0$, $\mathrm{ord}_Q(\tilde j - s) > 0$ and $\mathrm{ord}_Q(\tilde j_N - t) > 0$, then $P = Q$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the statement that a point of the plane model of $X_0(N)$ over $k$ which is smooth in the direction of the first coordinate is dominated by exactly one place of the modular function field; it is the first-variable companion of the corresponding second-variable statement. It is used in the analysis of the fibres of the plane model, where the place above a given smooth point is constructed and identified ([`ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_d2_of_derivative_evalEval_ne_zero_of_level`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_d2_of_derivative_evalEval_ne_zero_of_level)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CharPModel_place_eq_of_ord_pos_of_derivative_swapBivar_evalEval_ne_zero.lean

import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Bivariate
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JqCoeff
